                'slug' => 'kofejan',
                'summary' => 'To foster interactive real-time remote learning and ensure technology-based effective learning for underprivileged youth, CLP has established a remote teaching enabled Smart Classroom at Kofejan Nesa & Hazi Niamot Ullah High School, Kushtia on 23rd February, 2022. The school is located at Moslempur in a remote area of Bheramara upazila of Kushtia district. This school&apos;s students were behind the times when it comes to technology-based learning.',
                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">To foster interactive real-time remote learning and ensure technology-based effective learning for underprivileged youth, CLP has established a remote teaching enabled smart classroom at Kofejan Nesa & Hazi Niamot Ullah High School, Kushtia on 23rd February, 2022. The school is located at Moslempur in a remote area of Bheramara upazila of Kushtia district. This school&apos;s students were behind the times when it comes to technology-based learning. Bringing this smart classroom would allow 371 students (153 male and 218 female) to learn in an interesting and engaging atmosphere while also receiving lessons from skilled teachers and professionals. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/QFN32E-q3sw?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">This remote teaching enabled smart classroom is constituted of 1 laptop, 1 smart TV, 1 microphone, 1 IPS, and 1 camera, as well as other necessary components. Considering the present world, the majority of this institution&apos;s students will benefit greatly in the years ahead since they will be able to receive distance learning from skilled instructors all over the world via the internet. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset('root/assets/images/news/kofejan_plaque-min.jpg') . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"/><figcaption class="work_para_news">Plaque of newly established Remote Teaching enabled Smart Classroom at Kofejan Nesa & Hazi Niamot Ullah High School, Kushtia</figcaption> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">In addition, CLP has also reactivated a computer literacy center where students will now learn fundamental computer skills. This generous hand has been raised by the founder of this school Engr. Mohammad Abu Taher who is kind enough to contribute to the development of the disadvantaged. To successfully convey the current and technology-based education, Dnet&apos;s (CLP&apos;s implementing partner) official conducted a hands-on teachers training session for two teachers. Further, the head teacher of this school sincerely appreciates the patronage of this smart classroom for taking education one step further in his school.</p>',
                'date' => 'FEBRUARY 23, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => null,
                'image' => 'root/assets/images/news/kofejan_2-min.jpg',
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'A new CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom launched at Taher Secondary School, Kushtia',
                'slug' => 'taherschool',
                'summary' => 'CLP has launched a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and distance teaching enabled smart classroom at Taher Secondary School, Kushtia on 24th February, 2022 to extend modern ICT education among underprivileged youth in Bangladesh. The school is located in a remote area of Bheramara upazila in Kushtia district of Bangladesh. We cannot think in today&apos;s world without proper computer education to keep pace with the modern world.',
                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">CLP has launched a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and distance teaching enabled smart classroom at Taher Secondary School, Kushtia on 24th February, 2022 to extend modern ICT education among underprivileged youth in Bangladesh. The school is located in a remote area of Bheramara upazila in Kushtia district of Bangladesh. We cannot think in today&apos;s world without proper computer education to keep pace with the modern world. Currently there are 298 students (140 boys and 158 girls) are studying in this school. With the launch of this newly built CLC, 8 students every batch would have a place to study foundational computer skills with the support of “এসো কম্পিউটার শিখি (Esho Computer Sikhi)” book and trained teachers. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/KrvUgkTRmrY?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">The CLC center is equipped with 4 computers, 2 printers, and 2 UPS. At the same time, the distance classroom consists of 1 smart TV, 1 microphone, 1 laptop, 1 webcam and 1 IPS. The distance classroom will also facilitate as a multi-media enabled classroom, making learning more interactive and joyful to students. In additional, the incorporation of internet connectivity in this distance classroom will enable students in developing their English communication skills as well as obtaining learning from experienced teachers and experts all around the world. Engr. Mohammad Abu Taher, the school&apos;s founder, has sponsored both CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/taher_plaque-min.png") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Plaques of newly established CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom at Taher Secondary School, Kushtia</figcaption> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">The head teacher of the school expressed his acknowledgement, saying, "We genuinely thank authorities for giving computers and its accessories and teacher training to the school. Our students will go much further in ICT and become much more skilled in working with computers as a result of CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom activities.” He also admired the sponsor for his charity and compassion. </p>',
                'date' => 'FEBRUARY 24, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => null,
                'image' => 'root/assets/images/news/taher-min.png',
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'CLP has founded a new CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom at Sherua Adarsha High School, Sherpur, Bogura',
                'slug' => 'sherua',
                'summary' => 'On March 20, 2022, CLP established a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and Distance Teaching Enabled Smart Classroom at Sherua Adarsha High School located in a rural part of Sherpur upazila in Bangladesh&apos;s Bogura district to facilitate modern ICT education among disadvantaged youth.',
                'description' => ' <p class="work_para_news">On March 20, 2022, CLP established a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and distance teaching enabled smart classroom at Sherua Adarsha High School located in a rural part of Sherpur upazila in Bangladesh&apos;s Bogura district to facilitate modern ICT education among disadvantaged youth. Dr. Molla Fazlul Haque, one of the most valuable sponsors of CLP, has again reached out to disadvantaged youth by sponsoring these both CLC and distance teaching enabled smart classroom. At present 329 students (175 boys and 158 girls) are studying in this school. The CLC center is furnished with 5 laptops, 1 smart TV and other necessary equipment. In this newly constructed CLC, 10 students from each batch would have a place to master fundamental computer skills with the help of the “এসো কম্পিউটার শিখি (Esho Computer Sikhi)” book and trained teachers. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/DvvaE8K-noo?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">One smart classroom comprises of 1 laptop, 1 smart TV, 1 microphone; this smart classroom will function as a multi-media enabled classroom, promoting education more collaborative and interesting for students. On the other hand, the distance teaching enabled smart classroom consists of 1 laptop, 1 smart TV, 1 microphone, 1 webcam and 1 IPS. Moreover, the use of internet connectivity in this distance teaching enabled smart classroom would allow students to improve their English communication skills while also learning from experienced teachers and experts from all over the world. </p> <p class="work_para_news">Dnet&apos;s official trained 2 teachers of the school about CLP program to carry out the CLP activities smoothly and effectively. Along with that another 2 teachers were provided distance classroom management training through zoom meeting over the online. Nurul Islam Tarafder, the head teacher of the school admired the sponsor for his charity and compassion.</p>',
                'date' => 'March 20, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/DvvaE8K-noo',
                'image' => null,
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'Connect Students Around the world (CSAW) program held in collaboration with GK Adarsha High School and Great Oaks Legacy Charter School',
                'slug' => 'csaw-news-0',
                'summary' => 'Connecting Students Around the World (CSAW) was held in collaboration with GK Adarsha High School and Great Oaks Legacy Charter School on 26th June, 2022. This is one of the most fascinating CLP programs that has brought together students from these two schools to enhance their cross-cultural interactions and the development of understanding. The program was done through joint activities and live video discussions from the two different corners of the world.',
                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">Connecting Students Around the World (CSAW) was held in collaboration with GK Adarsha High School and Great Oaks Legacy Charter School on 26th May, 2022. This is one of the most fascinating CLP programs that has brought together students from these two schools to enhance their cross-cultural interactions and the development of understanding. The program was done through joint activities and live video discussions from the two different corners of the world. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/dtR8a1Lfbn4?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">GK Adarsha High School is located in Dhirasrom, a remote area situated in Gazipur district of Bangladesh. On the other hand, Great Oaks Legacy Charter High School is situated in Newark City of New Jersey, USA. Both schools have created and exchanged a story video to share their school life, daily activities and culture. Following that, students from both schools introduce and share their perspectives and knowledge via a live zoom meeting. Students and teachers are happy to be part of this wonderful program and to share their thoughts and culture. </p>',
                'date' => 'May 27, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/dtR8a1Lfbn4',
                'image' => null,
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'Another Connect Students Around the world (CSAW) program held in collaboration with Uddipon Badar Shamsu Bidya Niketon (UBSBN) and William Annin Middle School (WAMS)',
                'slug' => 'csaw-news-1',
                'summary' => 'Another Connect Students Around the world (CSAW) program was held in collaboration with Uddipon Badar Shamsu Bidya Niketon (UBSBN) and William Annin Middle School (WAMS) on 30th June, 2022. CLP launched the CSAW program in 2017 to increase cultural communication and develop understanding among young people living in different parts of the world. UBSBN is placed in a distant area of Bagerhat district called Chitoli and WAMS is located in the US state of New Jersey, far away from Bangladesh.',
                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">Another Connect Students Around the world (CSAW) program was held in collaboration with Uddipon Badar Shamsu Bidya Niketon (UBSBN) and William Annin Middle School (WAMS) on 30th May, 2022. CLP launched the CSAW program in 2017 to increase cultural communication and develop understanding among young people living in different parts of the world. UBSBN is placed in a distant area of Bagerhat district called Chitoli and WAMS is located in the US state of New Jersey, far away from Bangladesh. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/6-5850eL2yE?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">The program was held for the second time between the two schools. Students from both schools introduced themselves sharing their hobbies, cultures, school life through Book Creator - an online platform for creating and sharing books. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/csaw-news-1-img.png") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">After that, both school students participated in a live Zoom conference to get to know one another and address one other queries. Students and instructors expressed their desire for this program to continue in the future.</p>',
                'date' => 'May 31, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/6-5850eL2yE',
                'image' => null,
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'Pubali Bank Limited has partnered with CLP to empower disadvantaged youth through technology-aided education in Bangladesh',
                'slug' => 'csaw-news-1',
                'summary' => 'Pubali Bank Limited has partnered with CLP to empower disadvantaged youth through technology-aided education in Bangladesh. Pubali bank Limited has agreed to establish two computer literacy centers (CLCs). The CLCs will be established in Gazipur A. K. High School, Chandpur and KGS High School and College, Barishal.',
                'description' => ' <p class="work_para_news">Pubali Bank Limited has partnered with CLP to empower disadvantaged youth through technology-aided education in Bangladesh. Pubali bank Limited has agreed to establish two computer literacy centers (CLCs). The CLCs will be established in Gazipur A. K. High School, Chandpur and KGS High School and College, Barishal. Mr. Safiul Alam Khan Chowdhury, Managing Director & CEO of Pubali Bank Limited hand over the grant cheque to ATM Kamrujjaman, Joint Director of Dnet on June 16, 2022. Dnet is the implementation partner of CLP in Bangladesh. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/pubali-min.png") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Mr. Safiul Alam Khan Chowdhury, Managing Director & CEO of Pubali Bank Limited hand over the grant cheque to ATM Kamrujjaman, Joint Director of Dnet</figcaption> </figure></p>',
                'date' => 'May 31, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => null,
                'image' => 'root/assets/images/news/pubali-min.png',
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
            [
                'title' => 'CLP has established Computer Literacy Centers at Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School in Barisal and Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School in Chandpur',
                'slug' => 'pubalibank',
                'summary' => 'Computer Literacy Program (CLP) aimed to empower underprivileged youth through computer literacy education. Following that path, CLP has established a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and Smart Classroom (SCR) established at Belgachi Asiruddin Islmia Madrasah & Atimkhana & Lillah Bording, Belgachi, Chuadanga on 1st September 2022. The madrasah is located in a rural part of Chuadanga upazila in Bangladesh&apos;s Chuadanga district.',
                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">On 22th August 2022, CLP has founded a CLC at Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School and College, which is situated in rural parts of Bakerganj Upazila, Barisal. Currently about 486 students are studying in this school, out of which 246 are girls. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset('root/assets/images/news/1.jpg') . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Glimpse of CLC at Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School in Barisal</figcaption> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">Consequently, another CLC has also set up at Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School on 4th August 2022 in a far-off areas of Motlab upzilla in Chandpur. This school presently has 323 students, with 160 of whom are girls.</p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/2.jpg") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Glimpse of CLC at Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School in Chandpur</figcaption> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">Pubali Bank, one of the most prestigious banks in Bangladesh, has sponsored these two CLCs with the vision of CLP to empower the underprivileged youth through computer literacy education in these distant areas. Both CLCs are equipped with 4 laptop computers, 1 printer, 1 internet modem, and other equipment. A teacher&apos;s training was organized to explain CLC activities and give both CLC teachers introductory computer training. With the help of the trained teachers and the Eso computer sikhi book, eight students from a batch will be able to learn basic computer literacy from these two newly established CLCs.</p> <p class="work_para_news">Md. X, the X postion of Pubali Bank inaugurated the CLC at Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School and College and Md. Y, the position of Pubali Bank inaugurated the another CLC at Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School.</p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/3.jpg") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Glimpse of inauguration at Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School, Chandpur</figcaption> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">The principal of Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School and College, as well as the head teacher of Gazipur Kadir Aziz Lotif High School, expressed their heartfelt gratitude to the sponsor for unlocking the door to computer literacy education for their students. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/4.jpg") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"><figcaption class="work_para_news">Glimpse of inauguration at Krishnakathi, Goma, Sundarkathi Secondary School, Barishal</figcaption> </figure></p>',
                'date' => 'February 23, 2022',
                'youtube_url' => null,
                'image' => 'root/assets/images/news/1.jpg',
                'status' => 'published',
            ],
