                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">CLP has established a new Computer Literacy Center (CLC) at Sherpur Pilot Girls High School on 24th August, 2022. The school is located in a rural part of Sherpur upazila in Bangladesh&apos;s Bogura district. By establishing this CLC, Sherpur got another step towards expanding computer literacy among underprivileged girls. There are now 265 girls are studying in this school.</p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/1-min.jpg") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">The CLC center is equipped with 10 laptops, 1 printer and other necessary equipment. A teacher training program was organized to train the CLC teachers to impart modern computer education properly to the students. Under the guidance of trained teachers, 20 girls from one batch will be able to learn fundamental computer skills with the help of “এসো কম্পিউটার শিখি (Esho Computer Sikhi)” book. </p> <p class="work_para_news"> One smart classroom comprises of 1 laptop, 1 smart TV and 1 microphone; this smart classroom will function as a multi-media enabled classroom, promoting education more collaborative and interesting for students. On the other side, distance teaching enabled smart classroom have 1 laptop, 1 smart TV, 1 microphone, 1 webcam, and 1 IPS. Furhtermore, this distance teaching enabled smart classroom establishment and utilization of internet access will let students learn from expert instructors and professionals from around the world while also enhancing their English communication abilities.</p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/scr.png") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">The District Magistrate Md. Ziaul Haque of Bogura District inaugurated this CLC and SCR. At that time, UNO (Upazila nirbahi) officer of Sherpur upazila and other dignitaries were present. </p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/2-min.jpg") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">The head teacher of the school expressed his sincere appreciation to the sponsor (Dr. Molla Fazlul Haque) for opening the door of computer literacy education among the disadvantaged girls. More girls from this school will now be able to learn basic computer lessons.</p>',
