                'description' => '<p class="work_para_news">CLP has established a Computer Literacy Center (CLC) and Smart Classroom (SCR) at Darul Ulum Mohius Sunnah Madrasa, Begumganj, Noakhali on 12th September 2022 with the aim to empower underprivileged youth through computer literacy education. The madrasa is situated in a rural village of Begumganj Upazila in Bangladesh&apos;s Noakhali District. </p> <div style="box-shadow: 5px 5px 20px; border: 4px solid #f8f8ff;" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"> <iframe class="embed-responsive-item" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/5JdJCrkpiXk?autoplay=0&mute=0" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> <br> <p class="work_para_news">The newly opened CLC center is fully equipped with 3 desktop computers, 1 printer, and other appropriate infrastructure. A teacher training program has been organized to instruct CLC teachers in the proper delivery of modern computer education to students. A batch of 8 students can learn basic computer skills under the supervision of trained teachers.</p> <p class="work_para_news">About 178 underprivileged students are studying in this madrasa. Apart from that the Madrasa has an orphanage where orphan students get accommodation and quality education. To provide interactive and multimedia based education to the students, the smart classroom has 1 laptop, 1 smart TV and 1 HDMI cable and 1 IPS along with other necessary equipment. From now on students&apos; learning will be more effective, fun and enjoyable.</p> <p><figure><img src="' . asset("root/assets/images/news/noakhali-plaque.png") . '" alt="img" class="img-responsive"> </figure></p> <p class="work_para_news">Md. Riazul Islam, the madrasa&apos;s Muhtamim (Director), expressed his deepest gratitude to the sponsor for providing modernized and computer literacy education opportunities to the madrasa students.</p>',
